msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "See the `calendar.day` member for the individual day cells."
msgstr "有关单个日期单元，请参见 `calendar.day` 成员。"

#: css/calendar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [calendar.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/calendar/calendar.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [calendar.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/calendar/calendar.css)"

#: css/calendar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Expose the grid with `role=\"table\"` and a descriptive `aria-label`, and give each navigation button its own `aria-label`."
msgstr "使用 `role=\"table\"` 和描述性的 `aria-label` 暴露该网格，并为每个导航按钮提供其各自的 `aria-label`。"

#: css/calendar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The seven-column day grid."
msgstr "七列的日期网格。"

#: css/calendar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The month navigation row."
msgstr "月份导航行。"

#: css/calendar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A weekday column header."
msgstr "一个星期列表头。"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: callout"
msgstr ""

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`div[class~=\"instui-callout\"]` — Inline information alert for a short reminder or note."
msgstr "`div[class~=\"instui-callout\"]` — 用于简短提醒或注释的内联信息提示。"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "✅ Use Callout when:"
msgstr "✅ 在以下情况使用 Callout："

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- You need to highlight important information or reminders inline\n- The message is relatively brief (a sentence to a short paragraph)\n- The alert should draw attention without interrupting the main flow\n🚫 Don't use Callout when:"
msgstr "- 需要在内联中突出重要信息或提醒\n- 信息相对简短（一个句子到短段落）\n- 提示应引起注意但不打断主要流程\n🚫 以下情况不应使用 Callout："

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- The message requires interaction or multiple actions — use a Modal or Alert Dialog\n- The content is the main focus of the page — use a Card or Hero layout instead"
msgstr "- 信息需要交互或多个操作 — 使用 Modal 或 Alert Dialog\n- 内容是页面的主要焦点 — 改用 Card 或 Hero 布局"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- Ensure the alert role is properly applied (role=\"alert\" or role=\"status\")\n- Use semantic color contrast that meets WCAG AA standards\n- Don't rely on color alone to convey meaning"
msgstr "- 确保正确应用 alert 角色（role=\"alert\" 或 role=\"status\"）\n- 使用符合 WCAG AA 标准的语义颜色对比\n- 不要仅依赖颜色来传达含义"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Alert message content"
msgstr "提示消息内容"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Container for the text content."
msgstr "文本内容的容器。"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Optional icon to the left of the content."
msgstr "置于内容左侧的可选图标。"

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: card"
msgstr ""

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-card` — A surface container that accepts arbitrary content."
msgstr "`.instui-card` — 一个可容纳任意内容的表面容器。"

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Variant** controls how direct children are styled: `content` (default) leaves them\n  unstyled; `container` stacks them as bordered, padded sections. Padding scales with\n  viewport width and is the same across both variants.\n  **Size** is fully responsive — padding and border-radius step up automatically at 320px\n  (20rem) and 640px (40rem) via standard `min-width` media queries; no size class is needed.\n  Pair with `@pantoken/components` for heading, button, and other inline components."
msgstr "**Variant** 控制直接子元素的样式：`content`（默认）保持子元素无样式；`container` 将子元素堆叠为带边框和内边距的区块。内边距会随视口宽度缩放，并在两种变体中保持一致。\n  **Size** 是完全响应式的——通过标准的 `min-width` 媒体查询，在 320px（20rem）和 640px（40rem）处自动增加内边距和圆角；不需要额外的尺寸类。\n  可与 `@pantoken/components` 配合使用，用于标题、按钮及其他内联组件。"

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Use `<article>` as the card element when the card is a self-contained unit of content;\n  use `<section>` when grouped within a larger landmark. In `-variant-container`, prefer\n  `<section>` elements as direct children so each bordered region carries semantic meaning."
msgstr "当卡片是自包含的内容单元时，将 `<article>` 用作卡片元素；当卡片在更大的地标内分组时，使用 `<section>`。在 `-variant-container` 中，优先将 `<section>` 元素作为直接子元素，这样每个带边框的区域都具有语义意义。"

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Content card -nocard"
msgstr "内容卡片 -nocard"

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Container card -nocard"
msgstr "容器卡片 -nocard"

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Container card; direct children become bordered, padded sections."
msgstr "容器卡片；直接子元素变为带边框和内边距的区块。"

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Standard content card; children are unstyled. Default when no variant is set."
msgstr "标准内容卡片；子元素不带样式。未设置变体时的默认值。"

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- `@scope` is Baseline 2023 Newly Available; the card degrades to an unscoped flat stylesheet\n  in older browsers with no loss of visible styling."
msgstr "- `@scope` 属于 Baseline 2023 的新特性；在旧版浏览器中，该卡片会降级为无作用域的扁平样式表，但可见样式不会丢失。"

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [heading](/api/css/heading.md) — Place directly in the card or inside a container section.\n- [button](/api/css/button.md) — Place directly in the card or inside a container section.\n- [img](/api/css/img.md) — Place directly in the card as a media region.\n- [badge](/api/css/badge.md) — Place directly in the card as a status indicator."
msgstr "- [heading](/api/css/heading.md) — 直接放在卡片中或放在容器区块内。\n- [button](/api/css/button.md) — 直接放在卡片中或放在容器区块内。\n- [img](/api/css/img.md) — 直接放在卡片中，作为媒体区域。\n- [badge](/api/css/badge.md) — 直接放在卡片中，作为状态指示。"

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- https://drafts.csswg.org/css-cascade-6/#scoping"
msgstr "- https://drafts.csswg.org/css-cascade-6/#scoping"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: checkbox"
msgstr ""

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-checkbox` — A native checkbox and its label, or a switch via `-variant-toggle`."
msgstr "`.instui-checkbox` — 一个原生复选框及其标签，或通过 `-variant-toggle` 显示为开关。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Set `el.indeterminate = true` in JavaScript to show the mixed-state dash; the checked tick auto-contrasts against the fill — white on a dark fill, near-black on a light one. Also sets its own `gap` between the control and its label; chaining a `-gap-*` spacing utility modifier overrides that built-in value."
msgstr "在 JavaScript 中设置 `el.indeterminate = true` 以显示不定状态的短横；选中标记会与填充颜色自动对比——深色填充上为白色，浅色填充上为近黑色。还会在控件与其标签之间设置自身的 `gap`；对该内置值应用链式 `-gap-*` 间距实用修饰符可覆盖它。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [checkbox.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/checkbox/checkbox.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [checkbox.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/checkbox/checkbox.css)"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A native `<input type=\"checkbox\">` drives `:checked`, `:indeterminate`, and `:disabled`; set `el.indeterminate = true` in JavaScript for the mixed state, and note that `-readonly` is styling only since checkboxes have no native readonly attribute."
msgstr "原生 `<input type=\"checkbox\">` 驱动 `:checked`、`:indeterminate` 和 `:disabled`；在 JavaScript 中为不定状态设置 `el.indeterminate = true`，并注意 `-readonly` 仅用于样式，因为复选框没有原生的只读属性。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Invalid (error) state."
msgstr "无效（错误）状态。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Place the label after the control."
msgstr "将标签放在控件之后。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Place the label before the control."
msgstr "将标签放在控件之前。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Place the label above the control."
msgstr "将标签放在控件上方。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Read-only state."
msgstr "只读状态。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Show the required-field asterisk next to the label."
msgstr "在标签旁显示必填字段星号。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Render as a switch instead of a box."
msgstr "渲染为开关而不是方框。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The required-field asterisk."
msgstr "必填字段的星号。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "On `-variant-toggle`, the state glyph riding the handle: an X when off, a check when on."
msgstr "在 `-variant-toggle` 上，滑柄上的状态图标：关闭时为 X，开启时为勾。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The masked tick or dash glyph centered in the box; on `-variant-toggle` it becomes the sliding handle instead."
msgstr "居中于方框的被遮罩勾或短横图标；在 `-variant-toggle` 上则变为滑动的滑柄。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The box's mask glyph: a tick when checked, a dash when indeterminate."
msgstr "方框的遮罩图标：选中时为勾，不定时为短横。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The toggle border width."
msgstr "切换边框宽度。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The toggle switch height."
msgstr "切换开关高度。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The computed handle diameter."
msgstr "计算得出的滑柄直径。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The handle inset from each track edge."
msgstr "滑柄与每侧轨道边缘的内间距。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The toggle track width."
msgstr "切换轨道宽度。"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [radio](/api/css/radio.md) — The single-select counterpart."
msgstr "- [radio](/api/css/radio.md) — 单选的对应项。"

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: close-button"
msgstr ""

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-close-button` — A transparent icon button that draws its own × glyph, in three sizes plus an on-color variant."
msgstr "`.instui-close-button` — 一种透明图标按钮，会绘制自己的 × 符号，提供三种尺寸和一个有色变体。"

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Always renders as an icon-only control with no visible label, so an `aria-label` is required, not optional; compare to `button`'s `-without-background` ghost variant, which keeps a text label."
msgstr "始终以仅图标控件呈现且无可见标签，因此需要 `aria-label`，不是可选；可将其与 `button` 的 `-without-background` ghost 变体进行比较，后者保留文本标签。"

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [close-button.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/close-button/close-button.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [close-button.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/close-button/close-button.css)"

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Give the icon-only button an `aria-label` (e.g. \"Close\"), and mark a disabled button with `aria-disabled` (or the native `disabled`)."
msgstr "为仅图标按钮提供一个 `aria-label`（例如 \"Close\"），并使用 `aria-disabled`（或原生的 `disabled`）标记已禁用的按钮。"

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "For a close button placed on a coloured (non-neutral) surface."
msgstr "用于放置在有色（非中性）表面上的关闭按钮。"

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The × glyph, masked in `currentColor`."
msgstr "× 符号，在 `currentColor` 中作为蒙版。"

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [button](/api/css/button.md) — The general-purpose action button."
msgstr "- [button](/api/css/button.md) — 通用操作按钮。"

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: color"
msgstr ""

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.--text-danger` — Semantic colour utilities: `.--bg-<name>`, `.--text-<name>` (aliased as `.--color-<name>`), and `.--border-<name>` for the curated semantic palette. Every one of these also has a component-attached alias modifier (for example `-bg-danger` on any `.instui-<component>`)."
msgstr "`.--text-danger` — 语义颜色实用工具：`.--bg-<name>`、`.--text-<name>`（别名为 `.--color-<name>`），以及用于精选语义调色板的 `.--border-<name>`。每一个也都有一个组件附加的别名修饰符（例如任意 `.instui-<component>` 上的 `-bg-danger`）。"

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [generate.ts](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/scripts/generate.ts)"
msgstr "**Source:** [generate.ts](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/scripts/generate.ts)"

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Applies the semantic danger text colour."
msgstr "应用语义危险文本颜色。"

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Background colour utilities for semantic and component-aligned names."
msgstr "用于语义和组件对齐名称的背景颜色实用工具。"

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Border colour utilities for semantic and component-aligned names."
msgstr "用于语义和组件对齐名称的边框颜色实用工具。"

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Alias of `--text-*` for text colour utilities."
msgstr "`--text-*` 的文本颜色实用工具别名。"

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Text colour utilities for semantic and component-aligned names."
msgstr "用于语义和组件对齐名称的文本颜色实用工具。"

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: context-view"
msgstr ""

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-context-view` — An elevated callout with a caret, positionable on any side; works as a native `[popover]`."
msgstr "`.instui-context-view` — 带有尖角的提升型提示，可在任意一侧定位；作为原生 `[popover]` 使用。"

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The caret is two stacked `::before`/`::after` triangles (border then fill) so it reads correctly against a matching surface; as a `[popover]` it needs the same open/`popovertarget` wiring as `popover`, but unlike `tooltip`, it dismisses on outside click or Escape."
msgstr "尖角由两个叠放的 `::before`/`::after` 三角形（先边框再填充）构成，以便在匹配的表面上正确显示；作为 `[popover]` 时，需要与 `popover` 相同的打开/关闭 链接（open/`popovertarget`），但与 `tooltip` 不同，它会在点击外部或按 Esc 时关闭。"

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [context-view.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/context-view/context-view.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [context-view.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/context-view/context-view.css)"

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Dark (inverse) colour scheme."
msgstr "深色（反转）配色方案。"

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sit below the anchor."
msgstr "位于锚点下方。"

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sit at the end (inline-end) of the anchor."
msgstr "位于锚点的末端（inline-end）。"

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sit at the start (inline-start) of the anchor."
msgstr "位于锚点的起始处（inline-start）。"

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sit above the anchor."
msgstr "位于锚点上方。"

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Renders the caret's inner fill triangle."
msgstr "渲染尖角的内部填充三角形。"

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Renders the caret's outer border triangle."
msgstr "渲染尖角的外部边框三角形。"

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- Uses CSS anchor positioning (`position-anchor`, `position-area`, `position-try-fallbacks`) and the native `[popover]` API behind an `@supports` guard; needs a recent Chromium or Safari, and falls back to a UA-centred popover elsewhere."
msgstr "- 使用 CSS 锚点定位（`position-anchor`, `position-area`, `position-try-fallbacks`）和原生 `[popover]` API，置于 `@supports` 保护之下；需要较新的 Chromium 或 Safari，其他情况下回退为以浏览器为中心的弹出层（UA-centred popover）。"

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [popover](/api/css/popover.md) — The generic top-layer popover.\n- [tooltip](/api/css/tooltip.md) — A smaller hover or focus callout."
msgstr "- [popover](/api/css/popover.md) — 通用的顶层弹出框。\n- [tooltip](/api/css/tooltip.md) — 更小的悬停或聚焦提示。"

#: css/cursor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: cursor"
msgstr ""

#: css/cursor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.--cursor-pointer` — `cursor` as a composable, global class — `.--cursor-<value>` — usable bare or chained onto any component (`.instui-button.--cursor-pointer`)."
msgstr "`.--cursor-pointer` — `cursor` 作为可组合的全局类 — `.--cursor-<value>` — 可单独使用或链式附加到任何组件 (`.instui-button.--cursor-pointer`)."

#: css/cursor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [index.ts](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/utilities/cursor/index.ts)"
msgstr "**Source:** [index.ts](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/utilities/cursor/index.ts)"

#: css/cursor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "cursor: auto."
msgstr "cursor: auto."

#: css/cursor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "cursor: default."
msgstr "cursor: default."

#: css/cursor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "cursor: grab."
msgstr "cursor: grab."

#: css/cursor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "cursor: move."
msgstr "cursor: move."

#: css/cursor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "cursor: not-allowed."
msgstr "cursor: not-allowed."

#: css/cursor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "cursor: pointer."
msgstr "cursor: pointer."

#: css/cursor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "cursor: text."
msgstr "cursor: text."

#: css/cursor.md
#, no-c-format
