#: plugins/vite/workspace-orchestrator/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`@pantoken/vite-workspace-orchestrator` — a Vite dev-server plugin that watches upstream workspace\npackages and rebuilds them (and their dependents) when source changes."
msgstr "`@pantoken/vite-workspace-orchestrator` — 一个 Vite 开发服务器插件，监视上游工作区包并在源代码更改时重建它们（以及它们的依赖项）。"

#: plugins/vite/workspace-orchestrator/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "During development, changes to a local workspace package normally need a manual rebuild before the\ndev server reflects them. This plugin automates that: it watches each upstream package's source\nwith native `fs.watch` (not Vite's chokidar, which filters paths outside the project root),\ndebounces rapid changes, rebuilds in topological order, and registers built output with Vite's\nwatcher so the browser reloads. In pantoken's docs it keeps the generated CSS (`@pantoken/css`,\n`@pantoken/components`) fresh as you edit the libraries, instead of only at build time."
msgstr "在开发过程中，本地工作区包的更改通常需要手动重建后开发服务器才会反映。本插件将此自动化：它使用原生 `fs.watch` 监视每个上游包的源（而不是 Vite 使用的 chokidar，后者会过滤项目根目录外的路径），对快速更改进行防抖，以拓扑顺序重建，并将构建输出注册到 Vite 的 watcher，这样浏览器会重新加载。在 pantoken 的文档中，它使生成的 CSS（`@pantoken/css`、`@pantoken/components`）在编辑库时保持最新，而不是仅在构建时更新。"

#: plugins/vite/workspace-orchestrator/src/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "It applies during `serve` only, so production builds are untouched."
msgstr "它仅在 `serve` 期间生效，因此生产构建不受影响。"

